  "explanation": "Document D1S3 explicitly states that Guy Middleton was a citizen of the United Kingdom of Great Britain and Ireland (UKGBI), citing his birth in London in 1907 and the legal status of British subjects at the time. Document D2S3 asserts that he held dual citizenship, with the Kingdom of Italy being his second homeland, supported by evidence of his birth in Milan and official recognition of Italian citizenship in 1935. Both claims refer to the same individual and are independently supported by their respective sources. 'Kingdom of Italy' is used here as a specific designation of Italy during the relevant historical period and is distinct from the simpler 'Italy' in the R5 list, though both refer to the same modern nation-state. Since the question asks for the country of citizenship and both are valid under the cited sources, both are included."
